+
+## Final acceptance follow-up on 19 November
+
+Formal CI on `09352951d18f52f46a1f9144a29b93748bb0f1c6` finished with four of seven required contexts successful. Windows unit and Linux history paging failed; the aggregate remained blocked. Windows production E2E and both component phases succeeded. All required contexts, Storybook and review must pass on the final delivery HEAD before normal merge.
+
+Hosted quality trial `44480551654` completed full lint with zero errors, all 24 package typecheck tasks and App E2E typecheck. Its type graph used concurrency one and retained every task. The root typecheck script now adopts this serial graph. The trial's temporary lint memory settings are excluded from this change because its observed timings do not establish a performance improvement. The original shutdown signal's cause remains unclassified.
+
+The requester approved one migration exception: only PR #142 uses pre-integration V2 snapshot `928377ca374b85f4e1080b3ee836d4bb75c0fdfb` for incremental lint. The workflow fetches the exact merge SHA and verifies that snapshot is an ancestor before using it. Later pull requests still use their main merge parent. The six semantic rules and complete current-tree checks remain. The original main comparison contains 3,408 diagnostics; the snapshot comparison selects 131 diagnostics in integration-added lines. Historical diagnostics retain their complete external index. The existing generated-code exclusion policy now follows the Client generator's three actual output directories, accounting for 14 diagnostics in the original inventory. Generated files are unchanged.
+
+The paging trace separates observed native restoration from the idle-cache hypothesis. All 52 traced resize scroll writes correctly apply offset plus adjustment. Thirty unexpected base-point changes occur with idle state and zero accumulated adjustment; one chain restores the native offset from 84 to 2664, then a resize uses logical offset 84 and writes 131 after a correct +47 adjustment. The installed virtual-core fallback passes its cached offset to the existing application observer. Three real-timer cases reproduce that boundary directly: an actual scroll event delivers 84, the native position changes to 2664 without another event, and the idle callback incorrectly delivers 84. The vertical, horizontal LTR and horizontal RTL cases fail before the fix; four existing offset keepers pass. This identifies a concrete stale-value mechanism; final paging coverage still requires browser verification of the production correction.
+
+Temporary console, DOM-witness and geometry probes are archived outside the repository. The paging keeper returns to the exact `09352951d1` bytes, retaining its original actions, readiness, 80px minimum step, complete coverage assertions and failure attachment. Production timeline benchmarking completed on frozen pre-fix source `6ef67131e00575c3c1bd78185e65305fbd34cb54` before editing the observer. Run `44484576662` passes all nine entry, streaming and history-search samples with one worker and zero retries. Its helper bytes match the local pre-fix helper exactly. The final same-runner comparison remains required acceptance evidence.
+
+The observer now refreshes the native offset only when delivering idle state; active scrolling retains its event value. Reconnection checks use the same axis and RTL normalization. All seven offset keepers pass locally with 22 expectations, including the three real timers that failed before the correction. The patch uses the existing observer and native position, preserving the virtualizer's adjustment policy.
+
+Two remaining integration assertions are corrected at their existing owners. Mini transport's admission fixture copies readonly request arrays into mutable result arrays, preserving element values and the generated client's direct result shape; its 70 original cases pass with 194 expectations. Desktop's shared raw-row reader now verifies that each extension id is a string. An actual migrated SQLite database accepts a binary id in its non-STRICT TEXT column; before the fix, the early snapshot incorrectly exposes that binary value through the string bridge. The corrected reader skips non-string identities at that single raw-row boundary, keeping every valid string row and the existing strict current/legacy matching behavior. A mixed valid/binary-row fixture rejects the initial whole-read failure candidate and confirms the final reader preserves the complete valid snapshot. Thirteen window-snapshot and manager cases pass with 39 expectations, covering mixed invalid/valid rows, saved storage, and the original valid/current/legacy enable-state resolution. The enabled comparison remains exactly `row.enabled === 1`; no database data is rewritten.
+
+The remaining integration lint fixes make void returns explicit and reuse existing type-aware keys, record narrowing and Immer draft identity operations. Typed copy-on-write maps still return their owned objects. Independent review found one missed map registration; the existing model-plugin keeper fails with the missed registration and passes all six cases after its correction, with 47 expectations. Full typed lint and the approved snapshot increment will validate the complete frozen candidate in hosted quality.
